vms-a0c: alpha-dec-vms — a function ALIAS must also alias the procedure
ENTRY label ("..en"), so `.quad <alias>..en` in the .linkage pair resolves.

Third codegen-consistency defect in the alpha-dec-vms GCC 14.2.0 port, the
same class as vms-f97 one layer deeper: the entry label ("..en") of an
ALIASED callee.

musl defines many symbols via `weak_alias(old, new)` =
`extern __typeof(old) new __attribute__((weak, alias("old")))` and then calls
`new` in the SAME translation unit (src/env, src/exit, several src/complex
l-variants, ...). cc1 emits the value equate `new = old` (via ASM_OUTPUT_DEF)
— which aliases only the procedure VALUE — but every OpenVMS call site
references its callee through the .linkage pair as `<callee>..en`
(alpha_write_one_linkage, config/alpha/alpha.cc). Because `new` is a `.set`
equate, `new..en` is never a defined label (only the target's `old..en`
exists), so GAS rejected the object:

    $1..new..lk:
        .quad new..en          <-- Error: redefined symbol cannot be used on reloc
        .quad new              <-- OK: `new = old` resolves the value

~56 musl objects failed on exactly this.

Fix (minimal, precedented): the OSF/ELF alpha port ALREADY solves the identical
problem for its own entry label — config/alpha/elf.h's
ASM_OUTPUT_DEF_FROM_DECLS emits `$alias..ng = $name..ng` for a FUNCTION_DECL
alias so the normalized entry aliases too. The VMS port never defined
ASM_OUTPUT_DEF_FROM_DECLS, so do_assemble_alias (gcc/varasm.cc) fell back to
the plain ASM_OUTPUT_DEF and the "..en" entry was left unaliased. Define
ASM_OUTPUT_DEF_FROM_DECLS for OpenVMS to emit `<alias>..en = <target>..en`
for FUNCTION_DECL aliases (the OpenVMS spelling of the same idea), then emit
the normal value equate. TARGET has already been run through
ultimate_transparent_alias_target() in do_assemble_alias, so a recognized
C-RTL target correctly yields `decc$<name>..en`, matching the code entry label
alpha_start_function emits (vms-f97 / patch 0001). Non-function aliases are
unaffected (they have no "..en"). Verified: the EVAX assembler accepts the
"..en" equate and the reloc resolves.

This is internal-consistency only (the entry-label alias must exist wherever a
value alias does); the decoration/alias behavior itself is unchanged. Sanctioned
by the operator ruling to "make the port build" (path A to the Alpha DECC$SHR).

Clean-room (Rule 8): derived from public GCC source structure (the OSF/ELF
"..ng" precedent) + observed cc1/GAS output only; no VSI/HPE source consulted.

--- a/gcc/config/alpha/vms.h
+++ b/gcc/config/alpha/vms.h
@@ -247,6 +247,35 @@
     }                                           \
  while (0)
 
+/* vms-a0c (OVMX): a function ALIAS must also alias the procedure ENTRY label
+   ("..en"), mirroring how the OSF/ELF alpha port aliases the "..ng" entry
+   (config/alpha/elf.h's ASM_OUTPUT_DEF_FROM_DECLS).  On OpenVMS every call
+   site references its callee as `<callee>..en` in the .linkage pair
+   (alpha_write_one_linkage); when a function is defined via
+   __attribute__((alias)) / weak_alias, the plain `alias = target` equate
+   aliases only the procedure VALUE, so `alias..en` was never defined and GAS
+   rejected `.quad alias..en` ("redefined symbol cannot be used on reloc").
+   Without this macro do_assemble_alias (gcc/varasm.cc) uses the bare
+   ASM_OUTPUT_DEF and the entry label is left unaliased.  TARGET has already
+   been run through ultimate_transparent_alias_target() in do_assemble_alias,
+   so a recognized C-RTL target correctly yields `decc$<name>..en`, matching
+   the code entry label emitted by alpha_start_function (vms-f97).  */
+#undef  ASM_OUTPUT_DEF_FROM_DECLS
+#define ASM_OUTPUT_DEF_FROM_DECLS(FILE, DECL, TARGET)		\
+  do {								\
+    const char *alias_ = XSTR (XEXP (DECL_RTL (DECL), 0), 0);	\
+    const char *name_ = IDENTIFIER_POINTER (TARGET);		\
+    if (TREE_CODE (DECL) == FUNCTION_DECL)			\
+      {								\
+	fputc ('\t', FILE);					\
+	assemble_name (FILE, alias_);				\
+	fputs ("..en = ", FILE);				\
+	assemble_name (FILE, name_);				\
+	fputs ("..en\n", FILE);					\
+      }								\
+    ASM_OUTPUT_DEF (FILE, alias_, name_);			\
+  } while (0)
+
 #undef PREFERRED_DEBUGGING_TYPE
 #define PREFERRED_DEBUGGING_TYPE DWARF2_DEBUG
 
